  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 1, 'The Reference Architecture within planning and implementing a digital health enterprise' (Executive Summary). The infographic lists seven phases down the left, each with its steps: 01 Assessing the current state and enabling environment; 02 Establishing a shared understanding and strategic planning; 03 Defining the future state; 04 Planning the enterprise architecture; 05 Determining health content requirements; 06 M&E of digital health implementations and fostering data use; 07 Implementing, maintaining and scaling. Beside each phase are tiles for supporting resources, marked as PDF or online, such as the WHO-ITU National eHealth Strategy Toolkit, the Digital Implementation Investment Guide (DIIG), the WHO classification of digital health interventions, Open Health Information Exchange (OpenHIE), TOGAF, the Global Digital Health Certification Network, WHO SMART Guidelines (digital adaptation kits and machine-readable recommendations) and WHO FIC, ICD-11, HL7 FHIR and LOINC. A dashed box at the far right, labelled 'WHO-ITU Reference Architecture for DPI-H', sits level with Phases 01 to 04. A footer expands the abbreviations HIS, ICT, ITU, M&E and SDG.",
